title: HyperGSD Project Showcase
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

HyperGSD is a top-to-bottom re-architecture of the classic GSD5 plugin. It began with this initial goal:

* Eliminate typing and navigation lag on big GSD wikis
* End the reliance on deleting GSD actions to keep it performant, allowing actions to be kept for the long term
* Let GSD be freely mixed in with a general-purpose wiki.

By applying advanced TiddlyWiki optimisation techniques, such as Event Delegation, pure-HTML rendering, and strict index lookups, HyperGSD completely decouples the task-management UI from the global refresh cycle. It is virtually invisible to the CPU until you interact with it directly, thanks to `refresh.js` by Saq Imtiaz.

Having a much bigger wiki also led to questions on how to make about how to make it more efficient and useful. I

!! What's New?

* ''Multiple dependencies'': You can now have a list of dependencies against a single GSD action, with easy ways to add and remove them.
** While technically possible, contacts have been limited to just one, as a design decision to help productivity. If you are thinking you should list more than one contact, consider changing your action into multiple.
* ''Searchable pickers'': Projects, contacts, contexts and prerequisites are now chosen through a reusable popup picker (`$hgsd.pick`) instead of a flat dropdown. Type into the box to filter the list as you go. Project pickers (e.g. to select parent project) filter for titles and text default, while the prerequisite picker also searches body text and project name. Results stay grouped under their projects, with the current project shown first for convenience.
* ''Explicit contexts'': Contexts are now managed separately from other tags. They are deliberately not namespaced to GSD, and any page can become a context by tagging it with <<tag-pill GSD/Contexts>>
* ''Modal options'': The new HyperGSD tiddler modal now lets you choose the type, status, project, contact, context and realm of a new item before it is created.
* ''In-place editing'': Clicking edit beside a project or contact opens the picker pre-filled with the current value and focused ready for typing. Enter saves, Escape cancels without changing anything.
* ''ViewTemplate position toggle'': You can now instantly toggle the GSD Panel and Dashboards to appear either Above or Below the tiddler body directly from the HyperGSD Control Panel.

!! What Has Changed?

* ''"Frozen" refresh triggers'': Dashboards and ViewTemplates are now wrapped in `refresh` widgets that actively block updates during global actions (like typing in the search box). They only "wake up" if you modify a specific GSD item. This is the highest-impact of all changes.
* ''EventCatcher architecture'': Replaced hundreds of heavy individual checkbox and radio button widgets with a single, lightning-fast `EventCatcher` per dashboard list.
* ''Lazy-Loaded completed actions'': The Contact and Project ViewTemplates now feature a native "show completed actions" toggle, keeping the initial load time of large projects incredibly fast.
* ''Pure HTML rendering'': Dashboards now render using raw `<input>` and `<button>` tags controlled by CSS classes. This flattens the widget tree and allows TiddlyWiki to perfectly cache the parse tree of your dashboards.
* ''Tag-driven types'': HyperGSD relies 100% on specific tags (<<tag-pill $:/GSD/Action>>, <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Project>>, <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Contact>>, <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Reference>>) to identify items. This routes every database query through TiddlyWiki's ultra-fast C-level tag index rather than performing slow field scans.
* ''Statically-linked dashboards'': The "Dynamic Extensibility" loops that generated dashboards via shadow tags have been ripped out. Dashboards are now heavily optimized, hardcoded transclusions.
* ''Draft tiddlers are now excluded'' from lists, so you will not see a draft and the standard tiddler on refresh.
* ''Unified picker widget'': The Contact, Project, Prerequisite and modal dropdowns have been consolidated into one reusable `$hgsd.pick` widget — a single popup selector whose grouped lists are built from literal, statically-cacheable filter runs.
* ''Bulletproof checkboxes'': Status and completion doodads now use a robust conditional rendering strategy to explicitly remove the `checked` attribute when inactive, preventing browser rendering bugs.

!! What Was Removed?

* ''The `gsd_type` field'': This field is redundant under the new Tag-Driven architecture.
* ''The `gsd_perserve` field'': This was a typo carried over from old GSD5 code for a field that served no functional purpose.
* ''The `gsd_realm` field'': Realms are now plain TiddlyWiki tags, optionally assigned through the new modal.
* ''Prefix/suffix extensibility'': The legacy tags used to dynamically inject prefix/suffix icons into list rows have been removed, as the doodads are now hardcoded for maximum performance.